Z||000042||DRH||10-07-2001||03:52 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Mach10:<BR><B>Not to pick fights, but following the love thy neighbor logic, how do you explain all the nasty stuff that has happened in the name of God/Jesus? Religion as an instituition is a DANGEROUS thing, and should be treated as such. Ray's right, though a little foggy   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Stating that "all religion is dangerous" is about the same distance from genocide as stating "all non-believers are dangerous".  Some excellent examples of where this can lead can be found in China.<P>Any institution has the potential to be dangerous if it falls under the control of evil people. Whether or not it's based on religion is irrelevant. <P>The main reason there aren't more examples of atheist atrocities is that true atheist have been woefully outnumbered over the years. The odds are any madman is going to have some religious background. This will certainly be true if you attribute Hitler's actions to Catholicism.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>Quite a few atrocites have been commited by men that thought themself to BE god. Technically these people could be considered atheist since they didn't believe in any external diety...<P>||||reg||1
