Z||000072||Voytek||10-09-2001||06:13 PM||||Interesting discussion.  Let's see:<P>  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Religion is good. Without it we would not have come this far. What is bad are people who hide behind it. People who use it as an excuse to do evil. I have actually heard christians who have said "I am saved it does not matter if I do wrong I will still go to heaven". People that pick and choose what verses they remember are the problem. These people are not extremists. To me an extremeist follows a religion to the letter. Make no mistake what they do is not in any religious teaching. Dont bash religon bash the idiots abusing it. Simple Fiero grow up dude, hpefully that hatered will disapper.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Falconhulk - you're ABSOLUTELY right.<P>EdsB52 - first of all, I'm not going to get into everything you said - you talk too much! (not that you're not allowed to, just my opinion).<P>Second:   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>but in contemporary times it seems that people are killing the secular crowd with the rationalization of Christian beliefs. That doesn't mean Christianity is evil or that it is to blame, just that the tables of rationalization have turned.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Eds - try reading more than just your local newspaper every now and then.  Obviously you haven't heard that the hundreds of thousands of Somalians slaughtered in the last few years were primarily Christians killed for their beliefs.  In may African countries today Christians are being exterminated for their beliefs.  NO, the tables haven't turned.  Yes, certain Christian individuals have hidden behind the religion in the past and managed to lead others to comit attrocities against non-Christians.  The fact remains, Christianity was and is the most persecuted religion in the world.  I can find you more examples if you like.<P>Other than that, some of your logic makes absolutely no sense (I'm not just refering to your big words either).  You seem bent on questioning and attacking Christianity.  Do you know why you can do that?  Because you live in a country that was founded on Christian principles.  Had you been born and raised in the middle east, you certainly would not be able to attack Islam (and certainly not the Jews if you lived in Israel).<P>Oh, and the bible doesn't swear   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>With Christianity, if you question the Bible, God's existence, Jesus’ existence, or the history of the writings within the Bible, you will chastised, condemned straight to fncking hell<HR></BLOCKQUOTE>.<P>Christianity is based on principles good for absolutely everyone, no exception.  Only fanatics hide behind it (just like in other religions) and commit crimes.  If everyone was a true believer, people would forgive their enemies, do only good deeds and the society would be in a much better shape than it is today.<P>Having said that, I am a religious Christian and you've offended me with several of your comments.  To-date I have not seen so much hatred to a single group of people on this forum.  But since I am not an exemplary Christian, let me say this: I've never liked you but chose to ignore your pompous, self-self serving comments.  While others may be simply be misinformed or uneducated, you strike me as a complete ignorant a$$hole.<P>Unfortunately, ignorant, cocky pricks such as yourself are the most dangerous kind.  They hide behind big words and so-called intelligence, which often allows them to pull wool over people's eyes.<P>Try to educate yourself and cut down on Reader's Digest Word Power.<P>ray b - Can you say RUN-ON SENTENCES?????!!!!<BR>C'mon, say it with me: R-U-N O-N S-E-N-T-E-N-C-E-S.  There.  Now look it up.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by Voytek (edited 10-09-2001).]||||reg||1
