Z||000086||falconhulk||10-10-2001||10:05 AM||||Ray all your statements may be true.  I cant say either way until i look it up.  What I can say is that once again show me where in the bible the instructions on genocide are written.  Its not the religion thats bad its the teachers that are.  When the population cannot read they take for granted what they are told is the truth.  Like I said religion is good the people are bad.  The bible teaches that there are false prophets.  People will always lead others down the wrong path.  Its our responsibility to follow the right path no matter what and help others that have been led astray.  How can you condem a religion that as written is wonderful?  You are absolutely correct in saying that many atrocities are commited in its name.  Many more acts of kindness are commited that nullifies them.  You are the one who needs to think outside the box.  Sometimes we can fight so hard against the truth everything we see becomes a lie.  I am a christian.  I do not go around trying to get everyone saved.  I do not preach to people.  I will speak up when someone who has been misled speaks out.  Is 51 years of ignorance (lack of knowledge, not inteneded as an insult) not enough?  Open up and let other ideas in.  I find that many people who think like you are in a power struggle with the world.  You want to prove YOU control YOU and everything around you.  I think the proof of this is in the post that you mentioned having 59 people under you.  You live in a world were the only god is Ray.  Let me just say I feel you are intellegent.  Although I dont agree with your views I understand your arguments.  I like people who question the world.  Just ask yourself this "why do I associate the deeds of a misguided man with the written teachings of god"?  I think you will find that you have used these arguments for years to cover up the emptiness inside you and convince yourself there is no god.  Your argument is an internal struggle between your heart and your head.  Which one will win in the end?         <p>[This message has been edited by falconhulk (edited 10-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000087||Voytek||10-10-2001||10:34 AM||||Amen to that, falconhulk.  Well thought out.  Some good points from Tonker, too.<P>To keep a completely closed mind to religion is to live a life of emptiness.  Live and die - no hope.<P>I guess some messages can be conveyed without insults (*thinking happy thoughts*).    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Oh, one more thing.  Some people questioned the creation of the world in seven days.  What is a day in God's eyes?  Perhaps not 24 hours.  Maybe it's a million years?  My point is don't take it so literally.<P>Also, I realize that for many people it is hard to comprehend the existance of a supreme being.  Let me ask you: do you understand the universe?  Where does it end?  Where does it start?  What is beyond universe?  No one can answer that.  I'm not sure that there is anyone who can actually comprehend it.  If you can find anyone on this planet who can answer all of the questions above, you have probably found God.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by Voytek (edited 10-10-2001).]||||reg||1
