Z||000090||falconhulk||10-10-2001||01:07 PM||||Good selection Ray.  Like I said before I dont go around defending religon on a regular basis.  I dont have the bible memorized and I doubt either do you.  I would have to read those verses to respond.  What site did you pull that from?  A man who questions is not a heretic!  Maybe in the dark ages.  We should all question our faith to make it stronger.  In us all we poses a sense of right in wrong - put there by god.  One thing I have found is that athiests tend to have amunition ready to dispute everything that represents god.  I know if I did not think something existed and held no real value I would not research and fight to prove my point.  I would just think to myself "what fools they are".  Atheists tend to feel that way but also have this overwhelming need to recruit others to their side.  Kind of the same thing christians do but in reverse.  In the old testament God was a VENGEFUL god.  Thats were those quotes came from.  That all changed with the new testament.  The term "CHRISTIANS" means followers of christ.  The new testament is where christ gave himself for our sins and gods actions toward us changed.  I would prefer to keep this on an idelogical stand and not a specific verse quoting argument.  Your stance as well as others I have encountered appears to me as a call of help.  You want me or someone else to finally tell you what you need to dispute your long held disbelief.  You have one million reasons to think there is no god right?  All some men need to know that god exists is to think of thier families.  Would you really want your child to grow up in a world without a god?  Think back on your 51 years.  Think of the intense situations you have been through.....do you think god was not there to help?  No matter if we want him or not he is there.  He loves me no more then you.  The only difrence is you choose to turn your back to him.  As for your no god = no killing for gor think on this :  The pagans invoked the spirts of earth wind and other elements to bolster them against enemies.  When people feel week they use the most powerful thing they beleive in to bolster their courage.  Thats what those guys did on Sept. 11.  No matter if god exists or not EVIL in people will always exist.  God is the ONLY good that will combat that.  You are prtraying people as inherently being good and god twisting them to bad.  If thats the truth then life must appear as a real waste for you.  Men will always let you down, god will never let you down.  Try to build your own faith not tear down others.  I recently reread some of your earlier posts.  In response I want to say, I am a believer.  I dont hate you as an unbeliever or want to kill you.  I respect you  and your views.  I just dont agree.  My posts on religon are facts and your post are mostly veiled opnions.  I say vieled becasue they are intended to illicit the response this post received.  You want a debate not only make you feel supirior (In my opnion also in hopes that you will be proved wrong by someone before its to late) but to convince others.  Why do you feel the need to convince someone thier belief is wrong?  Is it so you will not be lonely?   <P>[This message has been edited by falconhulk (edited 10-10-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by falconhulk (edited 10-10-2001).]||||reg||1
